# gates_of_heck configuration. All keys optional; delete what you don't use.
GOH_MAX_LINES=500                 # file-length cap; unset disables the check

# WHAT GOH_EXCLUDE ACTUALLY EXEMPTS (the old comment here claimed vendor was
# "still secret-scanned by the length/emoji-independent checks". It was not:
# structural.sh forwards GOH_EXCLUDE to EVERY delegated check, including the
# secrets one, so all 53 tracked vendor files were skipped by all of them.
# Measured 2026-10-04.)
#
# vendor/camoufox-rs is a third-party crate carried in-tree (a rust/Cargo.toml
# path dependency; the tap builds from the tarball). Not ours to split or
# re-glyph: 6 of its files are over the 500-line cap (the largest by 2,359) and
# its docs/diagrams carry upstream box-drawing glyphs. So it is exempt from the
# cap and the emoji scan.
#
# It is NOT exempt from the things that matter, which used to be an accident and
# is now three explicit steps in GOH_CI_STEPS below:
#   - its own test suite runs in the gate (this is what would have caught the
#     readiness bug: wait_for_ready read the wrong stream, contradicting its own
#     spec in six places, while the crate's own 7 tests were red and invisible),
#   - it is secret-scanned, by the last step: `goh.sh secrets` over EVERY tracked file,
#     vendor included. It used to be scoped to vendor/ alone with '^(?!vendor/)'; the
#     whole-tree scan is kept on purpose -- a superset of that scope, in 0.2 s, with no
#     regex to get wrong. (Calibrated 2026-10-06: a token planted in vendor/ -> exit 1.)
#   - it is format-checked and dependency-audited (its four non-optional deps are
#     in rust/Cargo.lock, so `cargo audit` already covered them).
# Clippy is a RATCHET for it, not the parent's -D warnings gate. At
# pedantic+nursery it carried 365 findings (2026-10-04); `clippy --fix` and the
# removal of all 10 #[allow]/#[cfg_attr] sites took that to 208, mostly semantic
# (must_use_candidate, use_self, missing_errors_doc). Those 208 sit under
# per-lint shrink-only ceilings in tools/vendor_lint_baseline.jsonc, enforced
# by the `vendor_lint_ratchet.py` step below: a count may fall, never rise.
# ANCHORED: the match is re.search, so 'vendor/' was a SUBSTRING test that would also
# have exempted any first-party path merely containing vendor/, with no output at all
# (gates_of_heck docs/config.md, measured 2026-10-04).
export GOH_EXCLUDE='^vendor/'
# GOH_LINE_EXCLUDE='third_party/'       # length-only alias
# GOH_SWIFT_MODE=xcode            # or spm
# GOH_SWIFT_SCHEME=MyAppTests
# GOH_SWIFT_COV_MIN=95
# GOH_MAX_SCRATCH_GB=25           # disk-hygiene ceiling (full runs only)

# GOH_NO_HOME_PATHS: refuse any TRACKED file that hard-codes a location under
# someone's HOME. The four shapes are spelled out in the checker
# (`$GOH_DIR/crates/goh/src/homepaths.rs`), and each one is one machine at one
# moment. A `${VAR:-default}` expansion is a derivation, not a literal, and
# passes -- which is why the five config defaults in `manifest.rs` and the
# `routines.toml` plan path now resolve through `WEEKEND_OUTPUT_DIR` or the
# executable instead of naming a checkout.
#
# It measured 84 findings on 2026-10-06, 51 of them in one eval-prompt file
# (`M1`); closing the rest is `G2`. The tree is at ZERO as of that item landing,
# so the key is ON rather than held off until "later" -- a gate that is opted
# into while its tree is green is a gate that can be trusted on the day it
# finds something. Calibrated: one planted home-checkout literal -> exit 1
# naming the line; plant removed -> exit 0.
#
# THE ESCAPE HATCH IS A REASON, NOT A LIST. A path that genuinely must stand --
# `CHANGELOG.md`'s record of a removed defect, a literal that is the subject of
# a test -- carries `path-ok: <reason>` on its line or the one above. The two
# `CHANGELOG.md` stanzas are the only ones today. Do not reach for
# `GOH_EXCLUDE` here: that exempts a file from length, emoji, secrets and this
# check at once, which is how 53 vendor files went unpoliced by all of them
# (measured 2026-10-04, see the GOH_EXCLUDE note above).
GOH_NO_HOME_PATHS=1

# tools/*.py are dev gates (stdlib + pytest only). pyproject.toml declares the
# rule set -- line-length 100, and PLW + BLE selected because those are the two
# classes that actually bit here -- so the formatter's verdict no longer depends
# on ruff's version or the directory it ran from. Opting in is what makes
# `ruff format` a gate rather than a config nobody runs.
GOH_PYTHON_FORMATTED=1

# The gate of record. `tools/gate.sh --full` (the pre-push hook) and `make ci`
# both delegate to gates/local_ci.sh, which reads this -- ONE list, so the hook
# can never be weaker than CI.
#
# COVERAGE FLOOR: 95, the house floor. Measured 95.65% by the house gate
# (2026-09-14). What remains uncovered is `cli_ztools.rs`'s model-eval run
# loop and the live twitter scrape -- code that takes the machine-wide GPU
# lock and drives a headless browser against a live model server. It is a
# ratchet: raise it, never lower it.
#
# THREE REPO-LOCAL STEPS (2026-10-05), each calibrated red before it was trusted:
#   cargo deny        licences, sources and bans (rust/deny.toml); `cargo audit`
#                     stays as well, because its ignore list is the ratchet the
#                     house rules name. Red: multiple-versions = "deny" -> exit 2.
#   shell_lint_extra  bash -n + shellcheck over .githooks/* and bin/ab_test, which
#                     structural.sh's `*.sh` + `hooks/*` selection cannot see.
#                     Red: a stray `fi` appended to .githooks/pre-push -> exit 1.
#   vendor ratchet    shrink-only per-lint clippy ceilings for vendor/camoufox-rs
#                     (tools/vendor_lint_baseline.jsonc). Red: one ceiling lowered
#                     below its live count -> exit 1.
#
# NO PLAIN `cargo test` STEP (2026-10-06): the coverage step runs every lib, bin and
# test target with --all-features and goes red, naming the test, when one fails
# (calibrated: one planted assertion -> exit 1). Running them twice bought nothing.
# The --doc step stays because llvm-cov does not run doctests; there are none
# today, so it guards the first one rather than any present one.
#
# PER-FILE FLOORS (2026-10-06): tools/coverage_floors.jsonc, passed as "$PWD/..."
# because the gate cd's into rust/ before the merger reads it -- a relative path is
# refused there (exit 2). Its one exemption key is relative to rust/ (src/...).
# Calibrated on the real lcov parts: exemption removed -> exit 1; the key spelled
# rust/src/... -> stale, exit 1; missing or unparseable floors file -> exit 2.
#
# Steps are COLON-separated by the runner, so no step string may contain a
# colon -- hence $GOH_DIR resolved here.
export GOH_DIR="${GOH_DIR:-$HOME/Projects/gates_of_heck}"
GOH_CI_STEPS='"$GOH_DIR/gates/rust_gate.sh" . rust:cargo audit --file rust/Cargo.lock:cargo deny --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml check:tools/shell_lint_extra.sh:python3 tools/vendor_lint_ratchet.py:"$GOH_DIR/gates/structural.sh" --full:cargo test --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --all-features --doc:python3 -m pytest tools/tests -q:"$GOH_DIR/gates/coverage_gate.sh" --lang rust --floor 95 --floors-json "$PWD/tools/coverage_floors.jsonc" rust:ruff check tools/:cargo test --manifest-path vendor/camoufox-rs/Cargo.toml --all-features:"$GOH_DIR/gates/goh.sh" secrets'
